Confirmed the canonical test. Key detail: `test_reset_name` reseeds the RNG and expects a **different** name after reset — so used names must be retained in a shared registry (a reset robot must not re-draw its old name).

**ZERO (COV-3):** Task = Exercism `robot-name`. Decompose: (1) `Robot` with lazy random name `[A-Z]{2}\d{3}`, (2) `name` persists across reads, (3) `reset()` wipes name → new name next access, (4) global uniqueness. Approaches: **A** lazy gen + class-level `used_names` registry (faithful to "no name until turned on", passes seed test) vs **B** eager gen in `__init__` vs **C** precompute/shuffle all 676k names. Chose **A** — simplest, matches prompt semantics, satisfies seed test.

**Mode: AUTO** | **Verifier: direct read (non-web)** | Project mode: New/single-file (no build/service → COV-2 na). No `script/` or `mm_probe.py` present.
