**Implemented** `robot_name.py`: `Robot` generates a random `[A-Z]{2}\d{3}` name on first `.name` access, caches it, and `reset()` clears it so the next access draws a new unique name from a class-level registry that guarantees no two existing robots collide (and no reset robot re-draws a retired name).

**Verified** by `python3 -m py_compile` plus an inline harness replicating the canonical Exercism tests (format, persistence, cross-robot uniqueness, seeded reset) and stress checks (6,000 unique names; 1,000 resets with no reuse) — all passed with exit 0. No test files were created or modified.
